; Law 16(a), enforced: with nothing armed, a mutation-instrumented
; program is observationally identical to an uninstrumented one - same
; evaluation order, tail-call status, laziness, outcomes, counts and exit
; code. The method is the coverage semantics suite's
; (test/coverage_ppx/semantics/), with the coverage-registry assertions
; replaced by mutate-registry ones and one addition the coverage suite
; does not need: a SECOND compilation of the same sources with the
; rewriter switched off, so that every claim of "identical" is checked
; against a real uninstrumented twin rather than against an expectation
; someone could edit to match a defect.
;
; covsem_fixtures.ml is the coverage suite's fixture source, shared by
; copy_files as the RFC specifies (plain copy_files, not copy_files#, so
; that the file name the instrumenter records - and every mutant
; identifier built from it - names a file that exists in this build
; rather than one two directories away). It is frozen: read it, never
; edit it. mutsem_order.ml is the mutation-specific addition, and it is
; the one that settles the instrumenter's unproven claim that its
; right-to-left operand binding "matches the order the compiler already
; uses". mutsem_boom.ml is the third, and the only one the suite does
; not run: it exists to be run by the exit-code executables below, and
; to be catalogued here so that they are known to be comparing an
; instrumented program with a plain one.
;
; Nothing here sets an environment variable. The mutation runtime writes
; no file unless asked, installs no at_exit handler, and arms nothing
; unless WINDTRAP_MUTATE_ARM is read explicitly - which no executable in
; this directory does. That is itself part of what Law 16(a) claims, so
; the absence of a setenv is deliberate: an inert runtime should need no
; muzzling.

(copy_files
 (files ../../coverage_ppx/semantics/covsem_fixtures.ml))

; The instrumented half. The rewriter is applied unconditionally through
; (pps), as the coverage suite does, so no --instrument-with flag is
; needed for the law to be checked on every runtest.

(library
 (name mutsem_fixtures)
 (modules covsem_fixtures mutsem_order mutsem_boom)
 (preprocess
  (pps ppx_windtrap.mutate)))

; The suite is itself UNINSTRUMENTED, so its own definitions - and the
; baseline library it links - are the uninstrumented side of every
; comparison.

; windtrap.mutation: the suite links an instrumented library, and the
; discovery line after its summary is the loop's — the loop only
; answers where its library is linked (see lib/mutation/dune).

(test
 (name test_semantics)
 (modules test_semantics)
 (libraries
  windtrap
  windtrap.mutation
  windtrap.mutate
  mutsem_fixtures
  mutsem_baseline))

; The runtime-only link contract (Law 12, interchange contract): this
; executable lists mutsem_fixtures alone - no windtrap, no
; windtrap.mutate - and must still build and run, because
; ppx_runtime_libraries on the rewriter injects the mutation runtime the
; generated preamble calls, and nothing pulls the windtrap core in.

(test
 (name test_linkonly)
 (modules test_linkonly)
 (libraries mutsem_fixtures))

; The exit-code half of Law 16(a). mutsem_boom.ml is compiled twice, as a
; module of each library above; the two one-line executables below run
; the two copies of its [main], and BOTH outputs are diffed against the
; same committed golden, so the copies are pinned to each other and to a
; text a reviewer has read. with-accepted-exit-codes 2 is the exit-status
; assertion: OCaml's status for an uncaught exception, which an
; instrumented build must not change.
;
; The code under test is in the libraries rather than in the executables
; on purpose. A program that must print the same bytes whether or not it
; is instrumented cannot certify from its own output which of the two it
; is, so the certification comes from the registry - and the registry
; only sees what test_semantics links. Keeping mutsem_boom.ml in
; mutsem_fixtures puts it under that suite's "exactly these three sources
; registered" assertion and under its module coercion; an executable with
; its own (preprocess) field would have gone silently vacuous the day the
; field was dropped.
;
; OCAMLRUNPARAM is emptied so no backtrace is printed: a backtrace names
; the source path, the two copies live in different directories, and one
; shared golden would then be impossible for a reason that has nothing to
; do with the law.

(executable
 (name mutsem_exit)
 (modules mutsem_exit)
 (libraries mutsem_fixtures))

(rule
 (with-outputs-to
  exit_instrumented.actual
  (setenv
   OCAMLRUNPARAM
   ""
   (with-accepted-exit-codes
    2
    (run %{dep:mutsem_exit.exe})))))

(rule
 (with-outputs-to
  exit_plain.actual
  (setenv
   OCAMLRUNPARAM
   ""
   (with-accepted-exit-codes
    2
    (run %{dep:baseline/mutsem_exit.exe})))))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (action
  (diff mutsem_exit.expected exit_instrumented.actual)))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (action
  (diff mutsem_exit.expected exit_plain.actual)))
